{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066193-examples-of-patron-tools","id":1066193,"title":"Examples of Patron Tools","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-22T02:19:17-07:00","id":1066193,"title":"Examples of Patron Tools","content":"Patron Tool Yantras are magical tools given to the Seers of the Throne (or other people who bargain with powerful entities) that represent that Exarch's/entity's symbolism in the Fallen World. They can then use the tool as a Yantra. They are described as &quot;strings that puppet the Fallen World like a broken marionette.&quot; Each Exarch has a specific resonance that limits what magic can be worked by the Seer using that Exarch's blessing.<br /> <br /> What I'm wondering is: what exactly <i>are</i> Patron Tools? The heading of the Tool Yantras section says that magical tools are mundane items used to help work magic, but then the Persona Yantra is listed under the Tools section, and persona is more abstract than just simple mundane items. Are Patron Tools actual physical objects with symbols of the Exarch on them? Or are they more abstract, e.g. actions or deeds symbolic of the Exarch's dominion? A possible example of such abstract &quot;tools&quot; could be a Prelate of the General engaging in violence as part of a spellcasting ritual (self-flagellation, torture, attacking someone, whatever), or a Prelate of the Unity using his authority over a crowd as a Patron Tool Yantra in public speaking setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T02:57:49-07:00","id":1066205,"title":"","content":"In 1e they were a sacred word representing the Exarch that the individual Seer revered the most that they would place on...anything. A favorite method was to place it on things that the Pentacle typically used as Order tools in order to facilitate flying under the Pentacle's radar or for infiltration. I'd assume that the Patron tools work similarly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T03:09:37-07:00","id":1066209,"title":"","content":"If you wanted to make it a bit more thematic you could have Seers frequently use Patron Tools associated with their patron Exarch or ministries? I like the idea of a Mammon Seer who uses his credit card to cast spells, or a Praetorian who daubs sigils on his trusty Glock or knife.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T03:21:52-07:00","id":1066214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066193-examples-of-patron-tools?p=1066205#post1066205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 1e they were a sacred word representing the Exarch that the individual Seer revered the most that they would place on...anything. A favorite method was to place it on things that the Pentacle typically used as Order tools in order to facilitate flying under the Pentacle's radar or for infiltration. I'd assume that the Patron tools work similarly.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems those are the Seers' Order Tools in 2e. The book says, &quot;The Seers of the Throne each choose a sigil or word that they must display to use it as a Tool.&quot;<br /> <br /> The idea of mundane items that represent symbolism of the Exarchs is also good. Tying to the Ministries moreso than their Exarch patrons directly helps a lot because the Ministries (and even local cults of the global Ministries) all tend to have their own take on the Exarch they serve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T03:43:22-07:00","id":1066223,"title":"","content":"Just read the relevant parts in the 2e core again, Patron Tools are a subset of Order tools, so it is the name of the Exarch which they're using as a Yantra just like they used the name as their Order tool in 1e.<br /> <br /> The credit card or gun or whatever aren't the Patron Tool, but they would be appropriate receptacles for the Patron Tool which is the name of the Exarch. Like I said, the holy word/name/whatever you want to call it can go on anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T03:49:04-07:00","id":1066224,"title":"","content":"To me it looks like Patron Tools are under the same level heading as Order Tools, not a subset. Not that your interpretation is bad or anything, I'm just wondering what text you're using to support it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T05:15:18-07:00","id":1066242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>projectmoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066193-examples-of-patron-tools?p=1066224#post1066224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me it looks like Patron Tools are under the same level heading as Order Tools, not a subset. Not that your interpretation is bad or anything, I'm just wondering what text you're using to support it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what a subset is. Order Tools=General category, Patron Tools=Specific kind of Order Tool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T05:53:45-07:00","id":1066264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066193-examples-of-patron-tools?p=1066242#post1066242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's what a subset is. Order Tools=General category, Patron Tools=Specific kind of Order Tool.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What I'm saying is that both Order Tools and Patron Tools are at equal level under the Tools heading. The Patron Tool section does not appear to be a subset of Order Tools.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T06:00:50-07:00","id":1066266,"title":"","content":"Fair point, they all fall under Tools. I'll be honest I was eyeballing the header text for them both an d I could have sworn Order Tools was bigger and based my comment on that. Doh.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Patron Tools are some symbol or other granted by a Patron to a Mage that serves them. So they could be damn near anything, but I'd assume they have to be appropriately marked as belonging in the purview of that Patron.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T20:11:39-07:00","id":1066685,"title":"","content":"I believe Dave said that non-Seers can use Patron Tools if they happen to have them.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Ah yes, but it comes with yet to be known <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/850266-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-introduction-and-advanced-mage-sight?p=850509#post850509\">consequences</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-22-2017, 11:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T02:57:44-07:00","id":1066757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066193-examples-of-patron-tools?p=1066685#post1066685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe Dave said that non-Seers can use Patron Tools if they happen to have them.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Ah yes, but it comes with yet to be known <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/850266-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-introduction-and-advanced-mage-sight?p=850509#post850509\">consequences</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then they are most assuredly actual physical items.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T03:14:49-07:00","id":1066759,"title":"","content":"Well, nothing would stop a non-Seer from copying gestures, so the fact that non-Seers can use Patron Tools aren't conclusive proof. But they're Tools and I see no reason why they would differ from other Tools.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T07:14:53-07:00","id":1066849,"title":"","content":"Patron tools are the incorporation of symbolic resonance for the person's Exarchial/Abyssal/whatever patron. Physical objects are one form they can take, but they might also include a prepared environment or symbolic act.<br /> <br /> So, for example, a monitor set to observe feeds from security cameras would definitely count as a Patron tool of the Eye. Likewise, a Seer sworn to the Paternoster might stand in a high vestibule, listening to the chanting of parishioners below, praying to a false god and murmuring useless prayers, and use that to empower a spell as well.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T10:14:34-07:00","id":1066977,"title":"","content":"To my understanding,<br /> mundane items = Minitry (Order) tools, similar to Order Tools: Mammon can use credit cards as his Order tool.<br /> Patron Tools = Exarch's name/symbol, similar to High Speech, faster but specific: By invoking Mammon himself, seer empowers his spell <br /> <br /> I want tools to feel important. Sure a credit card is Mammon's (mundane) tool but isn't the headquarters of MasterCard a &quot;stronger&quot; Yantra since it combines both the concept of &quot;wealth&quot; (similar to credit card) but also &quot;control/authority of economic activity&quot;? Shouldn't a dramatic change is the Market (Apple's stock Price) be a stronger Tool than that of a rather common US dollar?<br /> Provided it is very thematic to the spell and situation at hand, I would rule a bonus dice of +2 (instead of normal +1) or apply a dice factor (9-again) on the dice roll.<br /> <br /> Thus, using Prelacy Yantras incoporates an Exarch's will into the spells Imago and by some extend the nimbus flare. That must be something detectable under Active Mage sight at the time of casting or at least later under Focused Mage Sight as enemy mages try to study it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6169-shadowjim12","name":"Shadowjim12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T11:54:44-07:00","id":1067051,"title":"","content":"Harder-to-acquire yantras usually get extra dice, yeah. Alternatively, you can borrow the rule about Mythic Places from Dark Eras and give a Mana reward for using places that are so grandly symbolic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T02:24:07-07:00","id":1067463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066193-examples-of-patron-tools?p=1066849#post1066849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Patron tools are the incorporation of symbolic resonance for the person's Exarchial/Abyssal/whatever patron. Physical objects are one form they can take, but they might also include a prepared environment or symbolic act.<br /> <br /> So, for example, a monitor set to observe feeds from security cameras would definitely count as a Patron tool of the Eye. Likewise, a Seer sworn to the Paternoster might stand in a high vestibule, listening to the chanting of parishioners below, praying to a false god and murmuring useless prayers, and use that to empower a spell as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is how I was originally going to implement the Patron Tool Yantra: more of a symbolic concept embodied in various objects or rituals rather than a single movement or mundane item. A Patron Tool of the Ruin might become active when the mage knowingly orders her followers to their doom and uses a Mind 3 spell to enhance their Athletics, or it might manifest as a mundane item or action: the mage signing a bill to destroy a housing project after falsely promising the tenants they would be able to stay would fall under the symbolism of the Ruin.<br /> <br /> In this case, the symbolism and resonance is the Tool, rather than any single item or action. For many Exarchs, the Tool can of course always be embodied in an item. The General might grant a weapon as a Tool. But that doesn't mean the Seer has to use that weapon to activate the Tool. They could just as easily perform an action that resonates with the General to gain the Yantra Tool bonus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T02:26:55-07:00","id":1067464,"title":"","content":"Since Patron Tool falls under the section that deals most with physical objects as aids to casting it probably shouldn't include actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}